-- Part 5: English Translations (Swami Sivananda & Swami Gambhirananda: 1,402 Records)
What use is dominion to us, O Krishna, or pleasures or even life?'),
('483eb606-f29d-5f52-981b-c41f88522d59'::uuid, '15ccce4b-d3fd-5030-a9f9-7453f30bb2c7'::uuid, 'gambhirananda', 'english', '- O Govinda! What need do we have of a kingdom, or what need of enjoyments and livelihood? Those for whom kingdom, enjoyments, and pleasures are desired by us—such as teachers, uncles, fathers-in-law, grandsons, brothers-in-law, as well as relatives—those very ones stand arrayed for battle, risking their lives and wealth.'),
('f168b113-4ee8-5833-8ca9-2ff54a967ca9'::uuid, '15ccce4b-d3fd-5030-a9f9-7453f30bb2c7'::uuid, 'sivananda', 'english', 'Those for whose sake we desire kingdom, enjoyments, and pleasures stand here in battle, having renounced life and wealth.'),
('57ca33b0-3b4f-5b48-a048-887613c47a15'::uuid, '05dc2578-7055-5593-aaae-281f754b7ead'::uuid, 'gambhirananda', 'english', '- O Govinda! What need do we have of a kingdom, or what need of enjoyments and livelihood? Those for whom kingdom, enjoyments, and pleasures are desired by us—such as teachers, uncles, fathers-in-law, grandsons, brothers-in-law, as well as relatives—those very ones stand arrayed for battle, risking their lives and wealth.'),
('290aa1fa-f0c9-548b-a617-0d14961e382d'::uuid, '05dc2578-7055-5593-aaae-281f754b7ead'::uuid, 'sivananda', 'english', 'Teachers, fathers, sons, and grandfathers, maternal uncles, fathers-in-law, grandsons, brothers-in-law, and other relatives—'),
('b8d478aa-62bb-5e67-81d3-60b988e2ae44'::uuid, '95f96233-748b-54e1-85c9-da49c51dc0ad'::uuid, 'gambhirananda', 'english', 'O Madhusudana, even if I am killed, I do not want to kill these even for the sake of a kingdom extending across the three worlds; let alone doing so for the earth!'),
('270f5f8e-fff2-550e-87c0-5f978aca7497'::uuid, '95f96233-748b-54e1-85c9-da49c51dc0ad'::uuid, 'sivananda', 'english', 'These I do not wish to kill, O Krishna, even though they kill me, for the sake of dominion over the three worlds; leave alone killing them for the sake of the earth."'),
('4207859e-059e-5507-9f80-a5efe685cfd6'::uuid, '19bcf343-fe9f-5d8b-9345-ac87f32830b7'::uuid, 'gambhirananda', 'english', 'O Janardana, what happiness will we gain by killing the sons of Dhrtarastra? We will only incur sin by killing these wrongdoers.'),
('49d5ac37-e449-5955-9cdd-d7016ef56666'::uuid, '19bcf343-fe9f-5d8b-9345-ac87f32830b7'::uuid, 'sivananda', 'english', 'By killing these sons of Dhritarashtra, what pleasure could be ours, O Janardana? Only sin would accrue to us from killing these felons.'),
('8040ed34-a2c5-581e-a2e9-080c5241b5a8'::uuid, '034ac013-6f5d-58d7-bc33-0f726dd77f58'::uuid, 'gambhirananda', 'english', 'Therefore, it is not proper for us to kill the sons of Dhrtarastra, who are our own relatives. For, O Madhava, how can we be happy by killing our kinsmen?'),
('03128001-ea23-52d2-831c-7570f035b934'::uuid, '034ac013-6f5d-58d7-bc33-0f726dd77f58'::uuid, 'sivananda', 'english', 'Therefore, we should not kill the sons of Dhritarashtra, our relatives; for how can we be happy by killing our own kin, O Madhava (Krishna)?'),
('15a35827-2c65-5e26-8b26-6586073f7566'::uuid, '767aba6c-fd8e-5d01-929a-c6b29b44164e'::uuid, 'gambhirananda', 'english', '- O Janardana, although these people, whose hearts have become perverted by greed, do not see the evil arising from destroying the family and sinning in hostility towards friends, yet how can we, who clearly see the evil arising from destroying the family, remain unaware of the need to abstain from this sin?'),
('5cfc680d-4e4a-5841-972d-74edf4b273f3'::uuid, '767aba6c-fd8e-5d01-929a-c6b29b44164e'::uuid, 'sivananda', 'english', 'Though they, with intelligence overpowered by greed, see no evil in the destruction of families and no sin in hostility to friends,'),
('a752073d-7e7a-59e6-86d8-9b5f6200f106'::uuid, '70e1c57c-7e35-5802-a24b-29af36a87d2c'::uuid, 'gambhirananda', 'english', '- O Janardana, although these people, whose hearts have become perverted by greed, do not see the evil arising from destroying the family and sinning in hostility towards friends, yet how can we, who clearly see the evil arising from destroying the family, remain unaware of the need to abstain from this sin?'),
('ce424bb9-af4c-54b6-90c9-fb6107cfe307'::uuid, '70e1c57c-7e35-5802-a24b-29af36a87d2c'::uuid, 'sivananda', 'english', 'Why should we not, who clearly see the evil in the destruction of families, learn to turn away from this sin, O Janardana (Krishna)?'),
('497c2d61-5bb7-51f5-804d-54979713651f'::uuid, '37083537-b98a-53eb-ae1d-6417c2b978ae'::uuid, 'gambhirananda', 'english', 'From the ruin of the family, the traditional rites and duties are totally destroyed. When rites and duties are destroyed, vice overwhelms the entire family.'),
('7a65229e-c56d-5c27-88b3-f0ae8499d5ac'::uuid, '37083537-b98a-53eb-ae1d-6417c2b978ae'::uuid, 'sivananda', 'english', 'In the destruction of a family, the immemorial religious rites of that family perish; on the destruction of spirituality, impiety indeed, overwhelms the whole family.'),
('d6c8c9aa-1600-5b03-8edb-8614372cf031'::uuid, '4d3b7f28-2042-59e2-bef8-7308ace03d9a'::uuid, 'gambhirananda', 'english', 'O Krishna, when vice predominates, the women of the family become corrupt. O descendant of the Vrsnis, when women become corrupted, it results in the intermingling of castes.'),
('aa1088e8-ec60-50b7-8690-27b30025ad39'::uuid, '4d3b7f28-2042-59e2-bef8-7308ace03d9a'::uuid, 'sivananda', 'english', 'O Krishna, by the prevalence of impiety, the women of the family become corrupt; and, when women are corrupted, O Varshenya (descendant of Vrishni), intermingling of castes arises.'),
('406de868-24c2-513e-b8da-51219b9c0c8e'::uuid, 'c35b1179-bfe6-595d-aa16-96b82d818384'::uuid, 'gambhirananda', 'english', 'And the intermingling in the family leads the ruiners of the family verily into hell. The forefathers of these fall down (into hell) due to being deprived of the offerings of rice-balls and water.'),
('dc91663f-afcd-5d54-9470-ec399532ad62'::uuid, 'c35b1179-bfe6-595d-aa16-96b82d818384'::uuid, 'sivananda', 'english', 'Confusion of castes leads to hell for the slayers of the family, for their forebears fall, deprived of the offerings of rice-balls and libations of water.'),
('1b76231a-7e62-55da-89ef-0166aeda70f9'::uuid, 'c9e2cec8-f68f-555d-83d3-e00463413f80'::uuid, 'gambhirananda', 'english', 'Due to the misdeeds of the ruiners of the family, which cause intermingling of castes, the traditional rites and duties of the castes and families are destroyed.'),
('a810a5d5-450a-5f02-b7db-4eff585478fe'::uuid, 'c9e2cec8-f68f-555d-83d3-e00463413f80'::uuid, 'sivananda', 'english', 'By these evil deeds of the destroyers of the family, which cause confusion of castes, the eternal religious rites of the caste and the family are destroyed.'),
('08cef174-2479-5d4e-94f1-e6e59385ed9f'::uuid, '4bb871c1-9cdb-55e2-aeb3-2e231713ab6a'::uuid, 'gambhirananda', 'english', 'O Janardana, we have heard that living in hell is inevitable for those whose family duties are destroyed.'),
('11611589-d243-509d-96b7-236004ce8b31'::uuid, '4bb871c1-9cdb-55e2-aeb3-2e231713ab6a'::uuid, 'sivananda', 'english', 'We have heard, O Janardana, that those men in whose families the religious practices have been destroyed are inevitably destined to dwell in hell for an unknown period.'),
('a9955be9-4e3c-5f3f-a04f-628dc323064a'::uuid, '31d28f6e-b44c-5a53-a501-104f7d5e516c'::uuid, 'gambhirananda', 'english', 'What a pity that we have resolved to commit a great sin, eager to kill our own kith and kin out of greed for the pleasures of a kingdom!'),
('3fb1182d-3355-5782-832b-77071440aa95'::uuid, '31d28f6e-b44c-5a53-a501-104f7d5e516c'::uuid, 'sivananda', 'english', 'Alas! We are involved in a great sin, for we are prepared to kill our kinsmen, out of greed for the pleasures of a kingdom.'),
('c2826981-f96b-5987-bc28-77988a8bd5ad'::uuid, '40d929a8-d7d2-537f-aad9-6bb98c26abdf'::uuid, 'gambhirananda', 'english', 'If, in this battle, the sons of Dhrtarastra, armed with weapons, kill me, who am non-resistant and unarmed, that will be more beneficial for me.'),
('f877e455-c9c5-52cb-9bd7-1304f6a53d55'::uuid, '40d929a8-d7d2-537f-aad9-6bb98c26abdf'::uuid, 'sivananda', 'english', 'If the sons of Dhritarashtra, with weapons in hand, should slay me in battle, unresisting and unarmed, that would be better for me.'),
('e8738d1f-666d-5cec-b64d-e271b455334f'::uuid, '70e2c09e-3b24-51ed-bb9a-0b42fb7f0717'::uuid, 'gambhirananda', 'english', 'Sanjaya narrated: Having said so, Arjuna, with a mind afflicted by sorrow, sat down on the chariot in the midst of the battle, casting aside his bow along with the arrows.'),
('4c08a320-f588-54d4-8a2e-b66ab8d6ee27'::uuid, '70e2c09e-3b24-51ed-bb9a-0b42fb7f0717'::uuid, 'sivananda', 'english', 'Sanjaya said, Having thus spoken in the midst of the battlefield, Arjuna cast away his bow and arrow and, his mind overwhelmed with sorrow, sat down on the seat of the chariot.'),
('192074c5-60b3-5e71-83ce-bc4e336065b0'::uuid, 'a61fd754-fbef-590c-9db2-3ffda51d5c95'::uuid, 'gambhirananda', 'english', 'Sanjaya said: To him who had been filled with pity, whose eyes were filled with tears and showed distress, and who was sorrowing, Madhusudana uttered these words.'),
('49dc0c2e-7cba-594c-be03-cfaa44c3abf2'::uuid, 'a61fd754-fbef-590c-9db2-3ffda51d5c95'::uuid, 'sivananda', 'english', 'Sanjaya said: To him, who was thus overcome with pity, despondent, with eyes full of tears and agitated, Madhusudana (the destroyer of Madhu) or Krishna spoke these words.'),
('bbe485ac-c0aa-5f72-a209-930f262c0511'::uuid, 'defcd45d-a454-5b6d-b4e3-b0ede64eb705'::uuid, 'gambhirananda', 'english', 'The Blessed Lord said, "O Arjuna, in this perilous place, whence has this impurity come to you, entertained by unenlightened persons, which does not lead to heaven and brings infamy?"'),
('1a55b033-a9b4-52aa-8e34-ef3ad406de8e'::uuid, 'defcd45d-a454-5b6d-b4e3-b0ede64eb705'::uuid, 'sivananda', 'english', 'The Blessed Lord said, "From whence has this perilous strait come upon you, this dejection which is unworthy of you, disgraceful, and which will close the gates of heaven upon you, O Arjuna?"'),
('69703047-7df0-565b-ac21-7b9045ac20f9'::uuid, '92802525-e007-5583-8e5c-aee82ac9beda'::uuid, 'gambhirananda', 'english', 'O Partha, do not yield to unmanliness. This does not befit you. O scorcher of foes, arise, giving up the petty weakness of heart.'),
('2af8ad13-f793-5837-b28c-267b6d98ba2b'::uuid, '92802525-e007-5583-8e5c-aee82ac9beda'::uuid, 'sivananda', 'english', 'Do not yield to impotence, O Arjuna, son of Pritha. It does not befit you. Cast off this mean weakness of the heart! Stand up, O conqueror of foes!')
